Toolbench bundles the following third-party open-source libraries. Each is
loaded only by the specific tools that need it, and runs entirely in the
visitor's browser.

- pdf-lib            — MIT      — https://github.com/Hopding/pdf-lib
- pdfjs-dist         — Apache-2.0 — https://github.com/mozilla/pdf.js
- fflate             — MIT      — https://github.com/101arrowz/fflate
- mediabunny         — MPL-2.0  — https://github.com/vanilagy/mediabunny
- gifenc             — MIT      — https://github.com/mattdesl/gifenc
- yaml               — ISC      — https://github.com/eemeli/yaml
- diff               — BSD-3-Clause — https://github.com/kpdecker/jsdiff
- marked             — MIT      — https://github.com/markedjs/marked
- qrcode-generator   — MIT      — https://github.com/kazuhikoarase/qrcode-generator
- jsqr               — Apache-2.0 — https://github.com/cozmo/jsQR
- cronstrue          — MIT      — https://github.com/bradymholt/cronstrue
- prettier           — MIT      — https://github.com/prettier/prettier
- @huggingface/transformers — Apache-2.0 — https://github.com/huggingface/transformers.js
- onnxruntime-web     — MIT      — https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime
- libheif-js          — LGPL-3.0 — https://github.com/catdad-experiments/libheif-js
- tesseract.js        — Apache-2.0 — https://github.com/naptha/tesseract.js
- tesseract.js-core   — Apache-2.0 — https://github.com/naptha/tesseract.js-core
- Tesseract tessdata language models — Apache-2.0 — https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata

Model weights are downloaded at runtime from the Hugging Face Hub only for
models on the reviewed, permissively-licensed allow-list in
`src/lib/ml/licenses.ts`; they are not redistributed with the site.

libheif-js (LGPL-3.0) is used by the HEIC tool only. It is loaded as a
separate chunk on demand, and the WebAssembly binary it needs is served from
this origin at `/vendor/libheif/libheif.wasm` (committed under
`public/vendor/libheif/`, with its licence text next to it). It is never
fetched from a third party.

tesseract.js (Apache-2.0) is used by the Image OCR tool only. It is loaded as
a separate chunk on demand, and everything it needs is served from this
origin under `/vendor/tesseract/` (committed under `public/vendor/tesseract/`,
with the licence texts next to it):

- `core/tesseract-core-simd-lstm.wasm.js` and `core/tesseract-core-lstm.wasm.js`
  — the Tesseract WebAssembly core, one with SIMD and one without.
- `worker.min.js` — the Tesseract worker script.
- `lang/*.traineddata.gz` — the Tesseract language models, copied unchanged
  from the `@tesseract.js-data/<lang>` npm packages. Those packages are
  published as MIT; the models themselves are the Apache-2.0 tessdata models
  from the Tesseract OCR project. `lang/NOTICE.txt` lists exactly which
  model each file came from.

Nothing in the OCR tool is ever fetched from a third party.

Build-time only (not shipped to visitors): astro, tailwindcss, typescript,
vitest, playwright, eslint.

Full licence texts are in the corresponding node_modules/<pkg>/LICENSE files.
